OBJECTIVE: Adversarially verify XBeach R1-G1 judgments. For each record in _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/verify/V-17.jsonl (ids in _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/verify/V-17.ids), try to REFUTE it against the original source. Read PLAN.md (schema/rules) in _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/ and CLAUDE.md "모델 분석 범위 통제" first.
SCOPE: READ-ONLY; modify nothing. Sources: models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/** and g1-20260930/generated/*.inc; indexes in runtime-20260912/, build-mode-20260912/build-map.json.
CHECK per record: (1) resolution correct? (e.g. wrong target, generic specific mismatched on arg count/keyword/optional/type/kind/rank, interface decl treated as definition, name-based intrinsic/external, array misread as call, missing host/internal scope option); (2) bindings complete? (missing condition-dependent alternative definitions, missing generated specific); (3) applicability correct? (build inclusion per family from build-map, CPP expression and its value, runtime condition incl. single-line IF, ELSE negation, prior return/exit/stop); (4) evidence actually supports the claim (not just a matching quote).
VERDICT per record: STANDS | NARROWED (core right, some field wrong/incomplete — say which) | REFUTED (resolution or target wrong). Give file:line + quote for every NARROWED/REFUTED.
STOP CONDITION: all records checked; no scope expansion.
DELIVERABLE: final message with one fenced json block: [{"id","verdict","field","problem","evidence","fix"}] listing ALL records (STANDS may have empty problem), then counts and any systematic pattern (a rule the judge keeps getting wrong).
